  "_comment": "Creatures from the 5e SRD 5.1 (CC BY 4.0), stats as published; balance.json enemyHpMultiplier scales HP at spawn. saveMod is the DEX save. Tier 1 = normal, 2 = elite, 3 = boss. minDepth keeps an enemy out of earlier Depths. 'big': true marks a heavy attack (bolt icon) that triggers a timed reaction when it hits. 'fx' on an attack intent picks its hit effect (slash, smash, stab, bite, arrow). Round 8: bosses: the tier-3 enemy whose minDepth is the Depth (Ogre 1, Owlbear 2, Young Green Dragon 3). Intent extras (game-side): 'extra' dice + 'extraType' on a hit; 'poison'/'poisonRounds' poison the target on a hit; 'area' hits every hero, with 'save' (CON|DEX) vs 'saveDc' for half; 'recharge' 5 = Recharge 5-6; 'damageScale' and the enemy's 'hpScale' scale the published numbers for a party of three (the Giant Wolf Spider's poison bite is modelled as 2 poison for 2 turns). Round 10: the Mimic (SRD 5.1) only appears from treasure that bites back ('random': false keeps it out of random groups). Round 11 (5 Depths): 'type' (undead\u2026) for Smite and cards; 'maxDepth' retires weak normals; 'maxAdds' caps a boss/elite's extra normals; 'regen' (+ 'regenStoppedBy' damage types) heals at the start of its turn; Hydra 'heads' / 'severAt' / 'regrowStoppedBy'; Lich 'summon' (allies at a HP fraction, once). Intents: 'condition' (+ 'conditionRounds', optional 'conditionSave'/'conditionDc') on a hit or a failed save; a non-area intent with 'save' targets one hero with a save instead of an attack roll; 'drain' heals the attacker by the damage dealt; 'perHead' attacks once per head; 'legendary' intents are used as an extra turn at the end of each round. Bosses: Ogre D1, Owlbear D2, Young Green Dragon D3, Hydra D4, Lich D5 (the end). Game-side scaling (hpScale, damageScale, regen, save DCs) keeps published dice for a party of three; the big retune is round 12.",
